1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,403
Teacher midterm practice, question 14.

2
00:00:04,023 --> 00:00:08,699
In Figure 1, at which points is there non uniform plastic deformation?

3
00:00:10,399 --> 00:00:12,805
Necking begins at D, the tensile strength.

4
00:00:13,424 --> 00:00:17,747
E and F are on the falling part of the curve, inside the necking region.

5
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:21,814
So the deformation is non uniform at D, E and F.

6
00:00:23,414 --> 00:00:25,667
The answer is D: D, E and F.

7
00:00:26,487 --> 00:00:28,871
Do not pick only the fracture point.

8
00:00:28,871 --> 00:00:31,698
The whole region from D to F is non uniform.
